{"name":"Fresh Green","hex":"#69d84f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Newly produced or obtained; recent.","(of food) Not dried, frozen, or spoiled."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Recently; just recently; most recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Qingming Festival","blocks":[{"text":"The Qingming Festival or Ching Ming Festival, also known as Tomb-Sweeping Day in English, is a traditional Chinese festival observed by ethnic Chinese in mainland China, Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, Malaysia, Singapore, Cambodia, Indonesia, Philippines, Myanmar, Thailand, and Vietnam. A celebration of spring, it falls on the first day of the fifth solar term, also called Qingming, of the traditional Chinese lunisolar calendar. This makes it the 15th day after the Spring Equinox, either 4, 5 or 6 April in a given year. During Qingming, Chinese families visit the tombs of their ancestors to clean the gravesites and make ritual offerings to their ancestors. Offerings typically include traditional food dishes and the burning of joss sticks and joss paper. The holiday recognizes the traditional reverence of one's ancestors in Chinese culture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Ching_Ming_comforts_to_heaven.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qingming_Festival"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg/500px-A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg/1280px-A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg/500px-A_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Indonesian Chinese family pray for their deceased members at Qingming Festival of 2013 under the Heaven Gate of Sanggar Agung","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Indonesian_Chinese_Family_pray_for_their_deceased_members_at_Sanggar_Agung_Temple%2C_Surabaya.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg/500px-Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg/1280px-Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg/500px-Chonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Qingming at the cemetery by Kolkata Chinese","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChonghe_Dong_Cemetery%2C_Qingming_Festival_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Five_coloured_papers_on_a_grave_mound%2C_Bukit_Brown_Cemetery%2C_Singapore_-_20110326-02.jpg/500px-Five_coloured_papers_on_a_grave_mound%2C_Bukit_Brown_Cemetery%2C_Singapore_-_20110326-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Five_coloured_papers_on_a_grave_mound%2C_Bukit_Brown_Cemetery%2C_Singapore_-_20110326-02.jpg/1280px-Five_coloured_papers_on_a_grave_mound%2C_Bukit_Brown_Cemetery%2C_Singapore_-_20110326-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com